-- ==================== Melee Mods (Combat tab) ====================
-- How melee is reachable, all verified live:
--   * The equipped weapon sits in Character.Equipped as a Model, and carries a
--     "Hitbox" Part whose Size IS the weapon's reach. Measured: Pocket Knife
--     2.93 studs, Hatchet 3.40 - so reach is read live and is automatically
--     per-weapon, with no table of hardcoded numbers to go stale.
--   * mouse1click / mouse1press / mouse1release all exist in Matcha, so a swing
--     is initiated the same way a player initiates one. The server sees an
--     ordinary attack rather than a forged remote, which is both safer and the
--     only route that does not need AR2's obfuscated Networking remotes.
--   * Hitbox has no Touched signal and no GetTouchingParts in Matcha, so "in
--     range" is computed geometrically from the hitbox position instead.
-- Cooldown is NOT readable from the weapon - it carries no attributes and no
-- config - so it is a slider. Set it slower than the real swing rate; clicking
-- faster than the game allows just wastes clicks, it does not swing faster.
